    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 95,
        "text": "So, Daniel, you're running this memory and testimony study. What exactly are you testing?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "72b2d7f3ef5ab94c98495b0206f13f2a356de3d0a4f11d5e359c512b762cac2a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 104,
        "sourceEnd": 200,
        "text": "We want to know how confident witnesses are, and how accurate they are. Are they the same thing?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "5f68dcec539a65e7ebde6bd80595be8b4bc7babd0d9f546f551cdedca52d410b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 207,
        "sourceEnd": 249,
        "text": "Good question. What have you found so far?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "9d677ca15ce2471baba0fb4b8c498ff0d5572760bc30ab9a045eed806af40312",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 258,
        "sourceEnd": 378,
        "text": "Well, in our first session, we showed people a short video of a bicycle theft. Then we asked them to describe the thief.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "76e687475fd0ed24d6ebc11475d54492fc8e88003ec3019ef8612a139404cda8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 385,
        "sourceEnd": 412,
        "text": "And did they remember well?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b3dec57b50ac2d467bae81ac94aeaa29903b2e4d3f8e34d42b537e260fcc8aba",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 421,
        "sourceEnd": 546,
        "text": "Some did, some didn't. But here's the interesting part: the people who were most confident were not always the most accurate.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d61d583f1b48d6514629447192ac196630889d44ee616c3037544c3895fefa10",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 553,
        "sourceEnd": 614,
        "text": "That's a bit worrying. So confidence is not a reliable guide?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3902ae70bde7ccc24312d9658e3cd2115ed825950103706ebaaa528cce8d754b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 623,
        "sourceEnd": 713,
        "text": "Exactly. Although confident witnesses sound convincing, their memories can still be wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "123e427f9e973ae7c107c43657b35388f3ba0457919d8df8954430513864d5f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 720,
        "sourceEnd": 775,
        "text": "What about the way you ask questions? Does that matter?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "15e9d3dd32d4bbdf008684b81a9993102d6c525f373310d52c7c18e6c4f91cfb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 784,
        "sourceEnd": 869,
        "text": "It matters a lot. If you ask a leading question, you can change what people remember.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "33e4bba89c0fc699e32edb23257ce3150f26628f509a93fedf309863833316fe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 876,
        "sourceEnd": 900,
        "text": "Can you give an example?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4089cfc6de9c1439b227c0ef93ad3abda9dceff16fb567b7e6a4cb7f1e885d8d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 909,
        "sourceEnd": 1064,
        "text": "Sure. We asked one group, \"How fast was the car going when it hit the tree?\" And another group, \"How fast was the car going when it smashed into the tree?\"",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "10a246f0dcc16587605a5650b8b4c20e0ec7bfb586a910a44c2a223eac3c1d4b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1071,
        "sourceEnd": 1117,
        "text": "And the second group remembered higher speeds?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "37b3ecbe0c41ae2ddf2c42ca190c6f8b3f0b2f3104bdea534f8567f725f2bc46",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1126,
        "sourceEnd": 1195,
        "text": "Yes, they did. The word \"smashed\" made them think the car was faster.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f5c2c45ad24ac86805a6d76dc1c84b3b5707b6dfc4431e79f944cb4b7a09de54",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1202,
        "sourceEnd": 1251,
        "text": "So the question itself can create a false memory?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3d595d57e1c1d2d4682d43db74934a200159bb1333655e880663f3b3de1d4817",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1260,
        "sourceEnd": 1363,
        "text": "It can influence memory, yes. Because the brain tries to make sense of what it hears, it fills in gaps.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2e80c63b0f6e9f14aa66a01443ef94487ad7357275cf08317f92ccbc423f7bd2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1370,
        "sourceEnd": 1431,
        "text": "That's fascinating. But surely some memories are very strong?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "d74a5e79783933047c5014f98eb220407dc46d10edba7fa7127ce4f707a62b62",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1440,
        "sourceEnd": 1528,
        "text": "Of course. Some memories are strong and accurate. But even strong memories can be wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "370da40923094085a9f532367666938f6153d4998689538d8e2a2a699af8d51e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1535,
        "sourceEnd": 1584,
        "text": "What about the police? Do they use your findings?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "8938fc028514a2d305c5955617c369aaf55fe74dc90904e11b1a84ce9b0451b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1593,
        "sourceEnd": 1694,
        "text": "Some do. We run training sessions for officers. We tell them to use open questions, not leading ones.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2aeda223bb6ff3722cf4b0adf0cb318988db4a12a3dc8cab5ff0402ee4ab3f6c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1701,
        "sourceEnd": 1720,
        "text": "And do they listen?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "8bf8b8fed75fcf848b3f6d352bf81bd71fd6beca4e2c68e3f273462437330cf3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1729,
        "sourceEnd": 1837,
        "text": "Mostly, yes. But change is slow. Even though the evidence is clear, some officers still use the old methods.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "83c7cb5fc0732d8ec1b8af3f0473b8dcfaac410d842655bf9ab5c199717f23bb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1844,
        "sourceEnd": 1879,
        "text": "I see. So what's your main message?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7bb7e61e21f97ac3a6c659426238ea138c659dc1e241cd776313bd992124590a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1888,
        "sourceEnd": 2005,
        "text": "My main message is this: memory is not a video recording. It's more like a story we rebuild each time we remember it.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "7522da01e95f0931415efd5a7a3eedc080b65e16b47400c4eb7021d2f7576df4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2012,
        "sourceEnd": 2063,
        "text": "That's a powerful way to put it. Thank you, Daniel.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "990abf546d27a4273746cd695d7fc55ca00ca46d79691c0d506867509a843b18",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2072,
        "sourceEnd": 2088,
        "text": "Thank you, Maya.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "c1f96f71b12e906e16e1389356068c4e000b7b89127f0362432dd46fe0044499",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
